  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 126 PM CDT Sat May 30 2026\n\nHopefully, everyone is out taking advantage of this mostly sunny, \nbut warm, weekend. Highs will be in the mid 80s to upper 90s, with \nheat index values ranging from 95-102, with the potential for \nisolated locations over the inland Coastal Bend to near 105. These \ntemperatures will continue through the upcoming work week, leading \nto a low to medium risk of heat-related impacts across South Texas.\n\nA low to medium (20-50%) chance of showers and thunderstorms will \ndevelop Monday afternoon as the ridge dominating the forecast \nweakens, allowing shortwaves to move across South Texas each day, \nenhancing the afternoon seabreeze. Moisture will continue to \nincrease this weekend through Tuesday, with PWAT values increasing \nto nearly 2\". Moisture will linger through the week, keeping \nafternoon shower and thunderstorm chances in the forecast through \nthe end of the work week.",
